  "assertions": [
    "Address-Data containing NUL supplies Receive evidence only with Type1 and no extra children; empty/NUL-free values and later request relations retain existing behavior.",
    "Complete shared-budget root/group scans verify unique Vendor10415 ancestor/type/data instances, exact flags, four-byte type1 and the selected NUL-containing value.",
    "Owned quotes are 48+align4(data length) bytes: three minimal vendor group headers and the entire original padded Data, without type, subscription or sibling data. The selected quote can contain address bytes.",
    "ErrField and Vendor10415 path873/877/(886 or1201)/897 remain. Build/Send and mixed extra children retain their original errors; ErrUnsupported is not added.",
    "Wrong type with NUL-containing value retains its prior unsupported classification; the old isolated type diagnostic remains covered independently.",
    "Structural and earlier wire/group failures retain priority, while later request constraints remain later. Reordering the address group after a malformed MMS scalar preserves first-failure order.",
    "NUL positions, signed type extremes, exact and one-less budgets, malformed instances, child order, padding, counters and ownership are covered.",
    "TCP/TLS ordinary/emergency/default paths verify exact envelopes, non-delivery, held charges, follow-up and retirement; a short emergency reply budget closes without truncation.",
    "Local affected-target fuzz and hosted17-target receipts are counted separately. Expanded local20-round regression uses a15-minute total test ceiling; release/fuzz budgets are unchanged.",
    "Pure Go, application-owned persistence, frozen rc.1 receipts, module requirements and immutable tags remain unchanged.",
    "Both address groups preserve first-failure order; an earlier address NUL supplies its own quote before a later MMS key NUL. General/balance cover their existing Originator-Address; submission-time mutation cases apply only to SMS templates."
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "Other existing conditional/value rules (including request relations, MMS field exclusions and subscription/SMS C-string constraints), mixed values/omissions and unreviewed group/cardinality/domain/handshake/header mappings remain separate. Keep safe close when no reviewed diagnostic applies.",
    "The changed development checkout needs a future immutable version and fresh core/adapter/cold-install acceptance. The verified rc.1 receipt remains valid only for its frozen commits.",
    "External private-template/target-recovery/role evidence and declared long-soak/saturation/tenant/mixed-transport acceptance remain separate."
  ],
